## TypeScript API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to provide a flexible and intuitive way for developers to control 3D camera animations in TypeScript, balancing ease of use with comprehensive functionality.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing all animation aspects. Instances represent individual cameras.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, initialCamera: THREE.Camera) {
           this.scene = scene;
           this.camera = initialCamera; // Underlying THREE.js Camera
           this.animationQueue = []; // Stores queued animation instructions
           this.isPlaying = false; 
       }

       // Animation Definition & Scheduling:
       addAnimation(animation: AnimationSpec): void {
           this.animationQueue.push(animation);
           // ... internal queue management (priority, timing, etc.) ...
       }

       playAnimations(): void {
           this.isPlaying = true;
           this.animateLoop(); // Internal loop handling playback
       }

       pauseAnimations(): void {
           this.isPlaying = false;
           // ... mechanism to pause active animation playback ...
       }

       // Camera Properties (Direct Access & Animation-Driven)
       get position(): THREE.Vector3 { return this.camera.position.clone(); }
       set position(newPos: THREE.Vector3) { this.camera.position.copy(newPos); } 
       get rotation(): THREE.Euler { return this.camera.rotation.clone(); }
       set rotation(newRot: THREE.Euler) { this.camera.rotation.copy(newRot); }

       //  ... additional getters/setters for FOV, near/far planes, etc. ...
   }
   ```

2. **`AnimationSpec` Interface (Blueprint for Animations):**

   ```typescript
   interface AnimationSpec {
       type: AnimationType; //  'linear', 'easeInOut', 'custom' (function)
       duration: number; // in seconds
       targets: { [property: string]: Keyframe[] }; //  position, rotation, etc.
       easing?: (t: number) => number; //  Custom easing function (for 'custom' type)
       onStart?: () => void;
       onComplete?: () => void;

